# Line endings are part of what this package ships.
#
# The gates read text files in the receiving repository and the scaffolder
# writes a shell hook that Git must be able to execute, so a checkout that
# rewrote either to CRLF would break a repository that this one never sees. One
# contributor on Windows is enough, which is why the rule is declared rather
# than left to each machine's `core.autocrlf`.
#
# `text=auto` still lets Git detect binary content, so nothing here forces a
# conversion on a file that is not text.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The hook is executed by name from `core.hooksPath`, and a shell script that
# lost its executable bit is a hook Git skips without saying so.
*.sh text eol=lf
pre-commit text eol=lf
